{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"I can assess it, but the report itself isn’t in the workspace—only RCA templates and guidance files are present.\n\nPlease attach the report (and, if available, its commissioning email or terms of reference) and tell me the relevant Australian state or territory. Privilege usually turns on:\n\n- the report’s dominant purpose when commissioned;\n- whether litigation was reasonably anticipated;\n- whether a lawyer requested or directed it;\n- who prepared, received, and circulated it;\n- whether it also served operational, regulatory, or patient-safety purposes; and\n- whether confidentiality was maintained or privilege may have been waived.\n\nA “confidential” or “legally privileged” label alone does not establish privilege. Until reviewed, avoid circulating the report further and obtain advice from the organisation’s lawyer."}}
